    "seconds": 43,
    "summary": "The anomaly is mitigated: `user-service` was scaled to zero replicas, which broke post composition, and it is running again.\n\n**What I found**\n- The `user-service` deployment was at 0/0 replicas. Events showed it had been scaled from 1 to 0 about 50 seconds after creation, and no pod was running.\n- No HPA exists, and the deployment carries no annotation explaining the change. Every other deployment runs 1 replica, so the zero was out of line with the Helm release.\n- Errors followed from this. `compose-post-service` logged `Connection refused` to `user-service:9090`, and nginx-thrift returned failures on `POST /wrk2-api/post/compose`.\n\n**What I changed**\n- Ran `kubectl scale deploy/user-service --replicas=1`. The rollout completed and pod `user-service-6d5985bd55-fqkwz` is 1/1 Running with a clean startup log.\n- The `user-service` endpoint is `10.244.1.246:9090`.\n- Since the restart (after <time>), nginx-thrift and compose-post-service have logged no errors.\n\n**Not verified**\n- I did not run an end-to-end post, follow, or login request, so the other operations are unconfirmed by test.\n- The mongodb index-creation errors in the logs date from 00:20 and appear to be startup timing noise. They were not investigated further.\n- I did not determine who scaled the deployment to 0. If that was deliberate, it should be recorded and the replica count managed through Helm so it doesn't drift again.",
